# Frontend Accessibility Regression (jest-axe + Playwright)

## Canonical helpers

| Layer | Module |
|-------|--------|
| Vitest | [`axe-test-utils.js`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/axe-test-utils.js) → `axeSeriousViolations()` (WCAG 2.x / 2.1 AA tags; **serious/critical** only) |
| Playwright | [`playwright_axe.py`](hpcperfstats/tests/playwright_axe.py) → `assert_no_serious_axe_violations()` |

## Trigger conditions

- New or materially changed **page shell**, **route layout**, or **modal/overlay** under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/pages/` or `Layout*.jsx`.
- New top-level SPA route that should appear in Playwright smoke (`_AXE_SMOKE_PATHS` in [`test_a11y_axe_browser.py`](tests/pipeline_e2e/test_a11y_axe_browser.py)).
- Overlay states users can open (Extended Search, histogram popover, staff menus with focus traps).

## Required behavior (Vitest)

1. Add or extend colocated `*.test.jsx` / `*.test.js` calling `expect(await axeSeriousViolations(container)).toEqual([])`.
2. Cover the **default loaded state** of the page or component.
3. When the component owns an overlay, also axe-scan with the overlay **open** (dialog shell for `ExtendedSearch` when tested outside `Layout`).
4. Run `npm test -- --run` under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend`.

## Required behavior (Playwright compose)

1. Add new primary routes to `_AXE_SMOKE_PATHS` when they are user-facing SPA entrypoints.
2. For lazy Bokeh or modal flows, wait for a stable selector (`role="region"`, `#extended-search-collapse`, etc.) before `assert_no_serious_axe_violations`.
3. **`test_web_pages_browser_e2e.py`** axe on an empty HTML probe is **harness-only** (validates the Playwright helper); **real SPA axe** runs via compose modules such as `test_a11y_axe_browser.py` and `test_job_detail_browser.py`.

## UX contracts (see also `wcag-aa-mobile-web.mdc`)

- **Bokeh:** never wrap `BokehEmbed` in `<button>`; use [`BokehPlotWithLimitation.jsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/BokehPlotWithLimitation.jsx) or Job Detail `PlotPanel` (`ariaDescribedBy` + visually-hidden limitation prose).
- **Dialogs:** match Extended Search in [`Layout.jsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/Layout.jsx) — `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, `aria-labelledby`, backdrop or `inert` on `#main-content`, `useFocusTrap`, Escape, restore focus; initial focus on primary field or title, not dismiss-only control.
- **Forms:** `aria-invalid` / `aria-describedby` must reference DOM nodes that exist (`ariaErrorProps` + `fieldFeedback` in Extended Search).
- **Tables:** `<caption>` (visually-hidden OK) and `scope` on `<th>`.
- **Color:** row/cell tint must not be the only cue; duplicate meaning in visible text or `aria-label`.

## Overlap

- **`wcag-aa-mobile-web.mdc`** — WCAG 2.2 AA and mobile layout when touching UI.
- **`testing-best-practices.mdc`** — pyramid layer selection; axe on page shells.
- **`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`** — web E2E assertion updates; WSGI probe disclaimer.
- **`bokeh-layout-surface-split.mdc`** — Bokeh embed timing and layout (not a substitute for limitation prose).
